# RentEZ — line endings.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true by default. Without the rules
# below, every shell script in this repository is checked out with CRLF line
# endings on a Windows machine, and bash then fails on the shebang line with:
#
#     ./scripts/smoke.sh: line 2: $'\r': command not found
#
# That error names neither line endings nor Windows, and it happens inside WSL2
# and Git Bash alike, because the corruption is in the checkout rather than in
# the shell. The same applies to the Makefile, to db/init/01-schemas.sql (which
# Postgres runs from a bind mount) and to scripts/gateway.conf (which nginx
# reads the same way).
#
# `* text=auto eol=lf` normalises everything to LF in the repository AND on
# checkout, on every platform, which makes each developer's autocrlf setting
# irrelevant. That is the point: this must not depend on four people configuring
# their machines identically.

* text=auto eol=lf

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ must be LF
# Called by a shell. CRLF breaks these outright.
*.sh        text eol=lf
Makefile    text eol=lf
mvnw        text eol=lf

# Read inside Linux containers from bind mounts.
*.sql       text eol=lf
*.conf      text eol=lf
Dockerfile* text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
.env.example  text eol=lf

# Kubernetes and CloudFormation. YAML mostly tolerates CRLF, but block scalars
# (the reaper Lambda's inline Python, the ALB fixed-response JSON) carry the
# stray \r straight through into the deployed artefact.
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- must be CRLF
# Windows batch files genuinely need CRLF; cmd.exe mis-parses LF-only scripts.
*.cmd       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf

# ------------------------------------------------------------------- binary
# text=auto detects most of these on its own; listing them stops a bad
# heuristic from ever corrupting one.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.ico       binary
*.jar       binary
*.war       binary
*.pdf       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
